[{"id":"VRCE-7-48-1","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":48,"verse":1,"english":"Beholding Sītā thus wailing, the sons of the Rşis there speedily approached the great Vālmīki, well-established in asceticism. And saluting him they all communicated to him Sītā's bewailing and said.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.775,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-49-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7048001","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ecfa1cc2be6651f2b92a774f4ada77a2d5fa30583bccc08bd6e138d4a1db7b76","compact":"9478df0e68dd7dba4643ef001e48cb4eec39833a162110c1c2061c8bc67aa4b7","nasal":"9478df0e68dd7dba4643ef001e48cb4eec39833a162110c1c2061c8bc67aa4b7"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-48-2","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":48,"verse":2,"english":"Beholding Sītā thus wailing, the sons of the Rşis there speedily approached the great Vālmīki, well-established in asceticism. And saluting him they all communicated to him Sītā's bewailing and said.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.892,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-49-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7048002","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b8ce14c869bd49409c142abb3717d38491e1e1512ae9f0b453d68ff32c1e6ae0","compact":"0af2c823ce4b7a55d4565e9cf56b1353e33cd23f9735a9d045ffad3b16a280ad","nasal":"0af2c823ce4b7a55d4565e9cf56b1353e33cd23f9735a9d045ffad3b16a280ad"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-48-3","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":48,"verse":3,"english":"O great Rşi, we do not know the wife of what great man, beautiful like the very Lakşmī, and not seen before, is crying aloud very poorly?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.923,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-49-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7048003","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7e168d85c20c8407af19d8aee4bc1585330b52c08febd97338bbba30e3d5bfac","compact":"b1939c1bfe1bbbff66fb8e7b2874fb8a363882954e6e22c5911d5a81c610edb1","nasal":"b1939c1bfe1bbbff66fb8e7b2874fb8a363882954e6e22c5911d5a81c610edb1"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-48-4","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":48,"verse":4,"english":"It is better that you should see her once. That beautiful damsel, like a goddess failing from heaven being bewildered, is waiting on the banks of the river.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.286,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-49-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7048004","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d0e461dd5a7f2165beea7d370192b804674d3ad095a810d2744126ccfc7ad527","compact":"626e7a4c7e40557b18679c47d27540c20b5f0d60708e59322aa47686a95383c8","nasal":"626e7a4c7e40557b18679c47d27540c20b5f0d60708e59322aa47686a95383c8"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-48-5","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":48,"verse":5,"english":"Hearing their words the great Vālmīki replied in worthy accents-\"This Sītā is the wife of the intelligent Rāma, the daughter-in-law of Daśaratha and the daughter of Janaka. She has now come to our hermitage. She is chaste and innocent, still her husband has renounced her. So we should all protect her.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.13,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-49-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7048005","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d7e0128b7048f1427491dae97bc55c16215015a348c6efcaf23581689760a54f","compact":"8e0b9dfa99fb23b3b07a69b7e316513645442ede48e28f19a63579e8ddfc0d6f","nasal":"8e0b9dfa99fb23b3b07a69b7e316513645442ede48e28f19a63579e8ddfc0d6f"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-48-6","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":48,"verse":6,"english":"You have seen, with your own eyes, the curse that the Brāhmaṇas have given me being enraged for a very trifling folly of mine.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.459,"method":"fuzzy-nearby-witness","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-54-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7048006","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7fe327650d5bb6694962d036da1130087b0c78e46598ed631066231c08cf677e","compact":"40ab3bf5fb46fa497b3c4c0da00c336b2cd6c6cc138f87bf202c119188c87357","nasal":"40ab3bf5fb46fa497b3c4c0da00c336b2cd6c6cc138f87bf202c119188c87357"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-48-7","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":48,"verse":7,"english":"Having gladdened a little the aggrieved Sītā by virtue of his own effulgence of the great ascetic Vālmīki addressed her in following sweet ascents. She did not appear to us to be a woman. Do you receive her duly. She is near the hermitage and so has come to seek your shelter.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.562,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-49-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7048007","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"30609f27e35f0aff952792a87d7717981a648e081f5291f50d1d572af5494c40","compact":"b0f62247d59a2d3126cb0d4d12ba92d3bef0054c3b1d59e9adee3673f514df0b","nasal":"d80a070289669d5a9889198572812c3b66506acf6b7d7893398bd8f73930fe1a"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-48-8","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":48,"verse":8,"english":"O chaste damsel, you at the daughter-in-law of Dasaratha, the beloved wife of Rāma and the daughter of Janaka; your coming here is auspicious. O illustrious Sir, she is on the look out for a protector-do you protect her.” The pious Vālmīki could perceive everything by virtue of his asceticism: and ascertaining the truth of the words of the Rși boys by the power of his understanding, he, with quick steps, approached Sita.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.825,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-49-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7048008","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"17502e3d737d3704613e67a8140cdbc5a861a6f889b6d8e0551eeedd1c636118","compact":"1d2745f6af62dfad1a3dc35e80c29c224c6b0b37232676feb84fbf054ade2082","nasal":"1d2745f6af62dfad1a3dc35e80c29c224c6b0b37232676feb84fbf054ade2082"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-48-9","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":48,"verse":9,"english":"I am apprised, by virtue of asceticism and meditation, of the object of your coming here. O great lady, I am also fully aware that you are by all means chaste. In fact I am conscious of all the incidents in the three worlds. And the disciple followed that high-minded ascetic. Thereupon proceeding a little on foot with Arghya in his hands, the wise Vālmiki reached the banks of the river and saw that Rāghava's spouse was bewailing like a helpless woman.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.831,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-49-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7048009","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6c2ebcbe1e0d8bd3032530b4896a93692fa7003bf53c435a782ac7b298e31b08","compact":"b713d39ac4d627cef97d603d639fa0b4fae7d7baae726fd9573137fb7fc245c0","nasal":"573f6b86a0e66928fc3d3db8d5e9bb97a5d97725e97272c0e60ec0e3ca385a14"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-48-10","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":48,"verse":10,"english":"By the eyes of asceticism, I perceive, O daughter of Janaka, that you are innocent. You have come under my shelter, O Vaidehi-to be you consoled.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.446,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-49-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7048010","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5f6d822d799663e6353cdde3dc9c7798b7685ed3d961d67a4ad429bd8999d216","compact":"650495